KG42.register("source_edge_archive-c0a1c6709a98e439de0752f0",{"id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R008::E::v141-c-R008-E002","paper":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","rule_ref":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R008","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R008-E002","source":"bidding.supply","target":"pricing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R008-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-05"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R008-C001"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"KG31-a9bd9e360b96ff06","target":"KG31-8571e493b8ecf84a","source_occurrence_id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R008::V::bidding.supply","target_occurrence_id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R008::V::pricing.local","source_unit_id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-a-M01::bidding.supply","target_unit_id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"Coordinator pricing in the P2P simulation framework and its SDR realization. | P2P framework under the stated passive-retailer assumptions. | SDR internal buying and selling prices at a given time step. | SDR internal pricing within one energy sharing region.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g07-ev-05"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"203637bfba476777f1c4b2f48f7977bec96ca66415f0be62407589669a33871a","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","source_definition":"The coordinator limits supply-bid updates by evenly randomly selecting a predefined-size set of participants forbidden to change their energy bids at each iteration. Scope: Optional bid-count step length control in iterative P2P energy bidding; selection covers all participants and applies to supply bids among their submissions. Condition: Bid-count control is adopted; the supply bid belongs to a participant selected into the forbidden set. The coordinator must reject a supply bid whose change exceeds the prescribed ramping-rate limit. Scope: Proposed practical coordinator enforcement of optional bid-ramping control in P2P energy bidding. Condition: The proposed enforcement rule is adopted and a supply bid exceeds the prescribed ramping-rate limit. SDR supply bids follow the energy-bid content specification in Formula (A18), derived from the participant's decision-making-model results. Scope: Supply quantities represented within SDR energy bids during the iterative bidding process. Condition: The energy bid is negative at the relevant time step. Supply-bid changes at each iteration must respect the prescribed ramping allowance around the previous bid, with the resulting bounds clipped to the minimum and maximum energy-bid limits. Scope: Supply energy-bid constraints in the simulation's iterative decision-making model. Condition: The bid-ramping form of optional step length control is adopted. The two controls may be combined by first limiting the number of bids allowed to change and then limiting changes to the allowable supply bids. Scope: Supply-bid updates under optional combined step length control. Condition: Bid-count control and bid-ramping control are used together.","target_definition":"Internal prices are tariff-bounded functions of the zone supply-demand ratio, with distinct buying/selling roles for net power signs. For SDR above one both equal the export tariff; for SDR between zero and one retain the source nonlinear selling-price formula and buying-price cost/balance construction. Do not generalize denominator limits or fee accounting beyond source conditions.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C001","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Submitted supply quantities, represented by negative net-energy bids, feed the regional supply-and-demand ratio used to calculate internal prices. Scope: SDR internal pricing within one energy sharing region.","expression":"\\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{PA}^-} \\left| e_{n,t}^{\\mathrm{bid}} \\right| \\quad \\text{with} \\quad \\mathcal{PA}^- = \\{\\, n \\mid e_{n,t}^{\\mathrm{bid}} \u003c 0,\\ n \\in \\mathcal{PA} \\,\\}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["theta-e-bid-SDR"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-05"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g07-ev-05","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p26-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":26,"printed_page":"1018","section":"A.2.1","anchor_text":"(A22) (A23) il price between the coordinator and the retailer as illustrated in Fig. 2; SDR haring r","equation_id":"A19-A23","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-26.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"With the energy bids from all the prosumers, the coordinator calculates the internal selling price by\n\np_t^{sell} = \\begin{cases} \\frac{r_t^{export} \\cdot r_t^{retail}}{(r_t^{retail} - r_t^{export}) \\cdot SDR_t + r_t^{export}}, & 0 \\le SDR_t \\le 1 \\\\ r_t^{export}, & SDR_t > 1 \\end{cases}  (A19)\n\nand the internal buying price by\n\np_t^{buy} = \\begin{cases} p_t^{sell} \\cdot SDR_t + r_t^{retail}(1 - SDR_t), & 0 \\le SDR_t \\le 1 \\\\ r_t^{export}, & SDR_t > 1 \\end{cases}  (A20)\n\nin which\n\nSDR_t = \\frac{\\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}^-} |e_{n,t}^{bid}|}{\\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}^+} e_{n,t}^{bid}}  (A21)\n\nwhere\n\n\\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}^- = \\{ n \\mid e_{n,t}^{bid} \u003c 0, n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A} \\}  (A22)\n\nand\n\n\\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}^+ = \\{ n \\mid e_{n,t}^{bid} \\ge 0, n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A} \\}.  (A23)\n\nIn Formulas (A19)-(A23), r_t^{export} and r_t^{retail} are the export and retail price between the coordinator and the retailer as illustrated in Fig. 2; SDR represents the supply and demand ratio of the whole P2P energy sharing region. Formulas (A19)-(A23) establish the pricing model in the coordinator agent under the SDR mechanism."}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"Coordinator pricing in the P2P simulation framework and its SDR realization. | P2P framework under the stated passive-retailer assumptions. | SDR internal buying and selling prices at a given time step. | SDR internal pricing within one energy sharing region.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g07-ev-05"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R008-E002","source":"bidding.supply","target":"pricing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R008-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-05"]},"paper_scope_note":"SDR, MMR, and BS are kept separate; the A18 net quantity differs from the A24 independent component; optional step-size control and the divergent loop in the example are not treated as general convergence or necessary dependencies."}});
